# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
*.egg

# Virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editable-install / setuptools artifacts
src/*.egg-info/
__editable__.*

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Bounds' own cache (regenerated; never committed)
.bounds/cache.db
.bounds/cache.db-journal
.bounds/state.json

# Per-tool agent configs generated by `bounds agent --sync`. The canonical contract lives in
# the committed AGENTS.md (the cross-ecosystem standard file); everything below is a regenerable,
# tool-specific pointer to it — kept out of the repo so a clone stays lean. Run `bounds agent --sync`
# locally to (re)create them for your editor/agent.
.claude/commands/bounds.md
.cursor/rules/bounds.mdc
.windsurf/rules/bounds.md
.aider.conf.yml
.github/copilot-instructions.md
GEMINI.md
# Per-agent native command/skill artifacts (also `bounds agent --sync` output, same policy).
.claude/skills/bounds/SKILL.md
.agents/skills/bounds/SKILL.md
.gemini/commands/bounds.toml
.opencode/commands/bounds.md
.github/prompts/bounds.prompt.md
.cursor/commands/bounds.md
.windsurf/workflows/bounds.md
# Claude Code invocation hook (`bounds agent --invocation nudge|strict` output). Same policy: a
# regenerable, Bounds-owned block merged into .claude/settings.json. (In a downstream USER repo this
# file is normally committed so the hook ships to teammates — here, like the rest, it's regenerated.)
.claude/settings.json

# Private design-vault stray docs accidentally dropped at the repo root. Internal idea-vault
# notes use `s-<N>-*.md` filenames and reference internal IDs (gen labels, premortems); they
# belong in the private vault, never in this public repo. Guard so they can't be committed.
/s-[0-9]*-*.md

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
